<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=revolver">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Weapons and war</p><h1 class="enc-title">Revolver</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as six-shooter, wheel gun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A revolver is a repeating handgun with a revolving cylinder holding several chambers, each aligned in turn with the barrel. The earliest examples of the modern revolver were made in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in the late 16th century, with a single barrel and a cylinder holding powder and ball, each chamber having its own flash-pan. A gun attributed to John Dafte from about 1680 is the earliest surviving example of automatic cylinder rotation. In 1836 Samuel Colt patented a revolver that became widely used and is credited as the first modern practical revolver, and in 1854 Eugene Lefaucheux introduced the first revolver using metallic cartridges.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/revolver.jpg" alt="Revolver" width="330" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Olegvolk at English Wikipedia. · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M&amp;Prevolver.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>late 16th century</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Germany</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>A revolving three-barrelled matchlock pistol in Venice dates from at least 1548, and a Tower of London matchlock revolver once believed to be 15th century is an Indian matchlock of the 1800s. Samuel Colt's 1836 patent is credited with the first modern practical revolver, though earlier similar examples existed.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/musket">Musket<span>by 1521</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=revolver">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
